      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Dam construction began in the late 1960s and was finished early in 1972, marking the lake’s birth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Holiday%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Between June 16 and 23, 1972, Hurricane Agnes dumped 19 inches of rain per hour, filling the lake to capacity in days.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Holiday%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A new spillway was added in 2013, costing residents over $10.5 million and reopening South Lakeview Drive on Memorial Day.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Holiday%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lake Holiday’s private marina serves only members, offering a quiet anchorage on the lake’s calm waters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Holiday%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The lake’s main inflows are Isaacs Creek and the combined Yeiders Run/Miller Run, feeding its 101‑hectare basin.",
